222	      <h1>Split clips</h1>
223	      <p class="desc">Cut clips in two at the playhead, and see what each piece keeps of the footage, actions, word timings and graphics.</p>
224	
225	      <p>Split cuts a clip in two at the playhead, so you can trim, move or remove one piece without touching the other. There's no separate blade or razor tool. Split does that job.</p>
226	
227	      <dl class="glance">
228	        <dt>Menu</dt><dd><strong>Clip ▸ Split</strong></dd>
229	        <dt>Keys</dt><dd><kbd>⌘T</kbd></dd>
230	        <dt>Where</dt><dd>The scissors button in the timeline bar</dd>
231	        <dt>Tools</dt><dd><code>split</code></dd>
232	      </dl>
233	
234	      <figure class="shot">
235	        <img class="light-only" src="../../docs/site/src/assets/screens/04-editor.window.light.webp" alt="The Frame Job editor window: a preview above a timeline, and an inspector down the right.">
236	        <img class="dark-only" src="../../docs/site/src/assets/screens/04-editor.window.dark.webp" alt="The Frame Job editor window: a preview above a timeline, and an inspector down the right.">
237	        <figcaption>A Shot: the capture at up to half its pixel width, a 1px line and the card shadow.</figcaption>
238	      </figure>
239	
240	      <h2 id="split-at-the-playhead">Split at the playhead</h2>
241	      <ol class="steps">
242	        <li>Move the playhead to the frame you want to cut on.</li>
243	        <li>Select the clips to cut, or select nothing to cut everything under the playhead.</li>
244	        <li>Press <kbd>⌘T</kbd>, choose <strong>Clip ▸ Split</strong>, or click the scissors button in the timeline bar.</li>
245	      </ol>
246	
247	      <table>
248	        <thead><tr><th>What's selected</th><th>What gets cut</th></tr></thead>
249	        <tbody>
250	          <tr><td>One or more clips</td><td>Each selected clip the playhead is inside</td></tr>
251	          <tr><td>Nothing</td><td>Every clip under the playhead on every unlocked track</td></tr>
252	        </tbody>
253	      </table>
254	
255	      <p>It's one undo step, named Split, however many clips it cuts. If nothing can be cut, Frame Job beeps and nothing changes.</p>
256	
257	      <h2 id="asides">Asides</h2>
258	      <p>The four Starlight asides, as the system's callout: a full tint, an icon and the word. No left bar.</p>
259	      <div class="aside note"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M10 2a8 8 0 1 0 0 16 8 8 0 0 0 0-16Zm0 3.5a1.1 1.1 0 1 1 0 2.2 1.1 1.1 0 0 1 0-2.2ZM8.8 9h2.4v5.5H8.8z"/></svg><div class="t">Note</div><div class="b">The cut lands on the project's frame grid.</div></div>
260	      <div class="aside tip"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M10 2a6 6 0 0 0-3.6 10.8V15h7.2v-2.2A6 6 0 0 0 10 2Zm-2.4 14.2h4.8V18H7.6z"/></svg><div class="t">Tip</div><div class="b">Select nothing to cut every clip under the playhead at once.</div></div>
261	      <div class="aside caution"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M10 2 1 18h18L10 2Zm-1.2 5.5h2.4v5H8.8zm1.2 6.3a1.2 1.2 0 1 1 0 2.4 1.2 1.2 0 0 1 0-2.4Z"/></svg><div class="t">Caution</div><div class="b">Sound fades are copied to both pieces, so set them again where you don't want them.</div></div>
262	      <div class="aside danger"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M10 2a8 8 0 1 0 0 16 8 8 0 0 0 0-16Zm-1.2 4h2.4v5.5H8.8zm1.2 7a1.2 1.2 0 1 1 0 2.4 1.2 1.2 0 0 1 0-2.4Z"/></svg><div class="t">Danger</div><div class="b">Reserved for what loses work. The docs have none today.</div></div>
263	
264	      <h2 id="with-an-agent">With an agent</h2>
265	      <p><code>split</code> cuts at a time you give it, or at the playhead if you leave the time out. See <a href="#">Tools: cutting and deleting</a>.</p>
266	      <div class="code"><div class="bar"><span>Terminal</span><span>Copy</span></div><pre><span class="c"># Connect Claude Code to Frame Job</span>
267	claude mcp add framejob -- "/Applications/Frame Job.app/Contents/Helpers/framejob-mcp"</pre></div>
